# Ansible collections installed into the image, one `<namespace>.<name>:<version>`
# per line. Comments and blank lines are skipped by the Dockerfile's loop.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT IS HERE IS DECIDED BY WHAT A CONSUMER'S PLAYS ACTUALLY USE, the same
# rule the Dockerfile states for binaries. These two are what the first ported
# play needed (ansible.posix for mount/sysctl/authorized_key, community.general
# for the package and service helpers ansible-core does not carry). Adding a
# third is a reviewed diff, because a collection is code that runs as root on
# somebody else's machine.
#
# Versions measured against the live Galaxy index on 2026-09-10: these are the
# highest published, and both declare a requires_ansible that ansible-version's
# 2.21.4 satisfies (community.general >=2.18.0, ansible.posix >=2.16.0).
ansible.posix:2.2.2
community.general:13.4.0
